   "html_text": "There are several ways in which a claim or a doctrine can deviate from what we require of science. Multicriterial approaches have the advantage over monocriterial ones that they can take this diversity into account. Bunge (1982, 372) asserted that many philosophers have failed to provide an adequate definition of science since they have presupposed that a single attribute will do; in his view the combination of several criteria is needed. However, in order to cover all ways in which one can devi",
